    "name": "Does a Backyard Cottage Need a Permit in San Diego or Chula Vista?",
    "text": "Does a Backyard Cottage Need a Permit in San Diego or Chula Vista?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "A backyard cottage in San Diego County may require a building permit because a detached unit with independent living facilities is generally treated as an accessory dwelling unit, but the exact process depends on the property’s municipality and site conditions. Before requesting a proposal, verify the jurisdiction, zoning, setbacks, utilities, fire-safety conditions, and whether the project is new construction or a garage conversion.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "Elite Remodeling & Design",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
